package game

/*
Room templates. Every room in the world is one of these blocks stamped into the
tilemap, so they all have to be exactly ROOM_W x ROOM_H characters.

	terrain                 spawn candidates
	  .  empty                E  enemy
	  #  rock                 C  chest
	  X  bedrock              o  coin
	  %  mossy surface        r  health rune
	  =  one-way platform     S  the player's starting flag
	  ~  water (deadly)       K  the boss key
	                          B  the boss

Spawn candidates are only offers: the generator decides how many of them a
particular room actually uses.

Two rules keep the generated world traversable, because doors are punched
through templates after the fact:

  - columns DOOR_X .. DOOR_X+3 must be clear on rows 1-2, and a platform has to
    be reachable below them, so a ceiling door can always be jumped into;
  - rows DOOR_Y .. DOOR_Y+2 must be clear along both side walls, so a side door
    always opens into standing room.
*/

ROOM_W :: 32
ROOM_H :: 18

// Where doors are punched. Side doors are three tiles tall and sit directly on
// the floor; ceiling and floor doors are four tiles wide and centred.
DOOR_Y :: 13
DOOR_H :: 3
DOOR_X :: 14
DOOR_W :: 4

ROOM_START :: `################################
